<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow" style="justify-content:center;">FAQ</span>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <svg class="arc-underline" viewBox="0 0 56 14"><path d="M2 2c8 12 44 12 52 0"/></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list reveal" id="faqList">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question"><span>How much do braces and Invisalign cost in Southampton, NY?</span><span class="plusminus"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Treatment costs vary depending on the complexity of your case. Braces typically range from $3,000–$7,000, and Invisalign falls within a similar range. We offer flexible payment plans with low monthly options, and we verify your insurance benefits for free before you commit to anything. Your complimentary consultation includes a full cost breakdown with no hidden fees.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question"><span>Is the consultation really free?</span><span class="plusminus"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Your initial consultation with Dr. Cartier is completely complimentary — a clinical exam, a discussion of your goals, a review of treatment options, and a clear explanation of costs, insurance, and payment plans. No obligation, no pressure.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question"><span>Do braces hurt? What about Invisalign?</span><span class="plusminus"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Most patients feel mild pressure for the first 3–5 days after braces are placed or after each Invisalign tray change — a normal sign treatment is working. Modern braces and aligners are gentler than ever, and 92% of patients say they'd do it again.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question"><span>How do I know if my child needs braces, Invisalign, or airway orthodontics?</span><span class="plusminus"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The best way to find out is a professional evaluation — the American Association of Orthodontists recommends children see an orthodontist by age 7. At your free consultation, Dr. Cartier assesses teeth, jaw development, and breathing patterns to recommend the right path. If treatment isn't needed yet, we'll tell you honestly and monitor growth at no charge.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question"><span>What is airway orthodontics and how do I know if my child needs it?</span><span class="plusminus"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Airway orthodontics looks at how jaw, teeth, and airway development impacts breathing and sleep. Snoring, mouth breathing, restless sleep, or trouble focusing at school can be signs. Dr. Cartier works with an onsite ENT specialist to evaluate these concerns — early intervention between ages 7 and 12 can prevent more complex treatment later.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question"><span>Do you accept insurance for orthodontic treatment?</span><span class="plusminus"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes, we accept most major dental insurance plans that include orthodontic coverage. Many plans cover 25–50% of treatment. Our team verifies your benefits and handles claims so you get maximum coverage, and we offer low monthly payment plans for any remaining balance.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question"><span>How long does orthodontic treatment take?</span><span class="plusminus"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Most braces treatments take 12–24 months. Invisalign typically runs 6–18 months for mild-to-moderate cases, and early treatment or palate expansion usually takes 6–12 months. At your free consultation, Dr. Cartier gives you a realistic timeline specific to your case.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question"><span>Why should I choose Cartier Orthodontics over other orthodontists in the Hamptons?</span><span class="plusminus"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>You'll see Dr. Cartier personally at every single visit — never a rotating associate. With over 30 years of board-certified experience, care for every age including special needs, airway-focused orthodontics with an onsite ENT, two Hamptons locations, and bilingual service, it's care that goes further.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

